section('ia','06 / Information architecture and page plans',sitemap+p('<strong>Desktop navigation:</strong> Products · Platform · Solutions · Pricing · Resources · Company · Sign in · Request demo. “Inspect sample claim” remains prominent in the hero and product pages. “Request a pilot” is the scoped commercial action. The product menu lists every offer by name and job; resources contains evaluation, comparisons and carrier rules.')+p('<strong>Footer:</strong> all five products; platform/features/workflow fit; all solutions; resources/results; company/contact; demo/pilot/access; privacy/terms; copyright. LinkedIn and Crunchbase icons require supplied profile URLs—show a labeled inactive state if none exists. Do not invent an address, phone number, staff, profile or domain.')+table(['Route','Page','Coverage','Unique hero / visual story','Next action'],routes)+p('<strong>Depth policy:</strong> product pages own commercial explanations; features owns capability detail; solutions own role-specific decisions; resources owns methodology. Shared content is summarized with links, not copied into repetitive pages. All routes above are planned routes, not implemented links in this report.'))

home=[
('H01','Know what’s missing. Before you file.','A provenance-first evidence audit for cargo damage and shortage claims. Explore one synthetic shipment with an unresolved POD signature, ambiguous photo date and conflicting draft value.','Crisp white architectural grid; central glass dossier connected to emerald cargo-owner cube, modular 3PL blocks and silver insurer frame; persistent CONCEPT PREVIEW.','On load: wordmark and navigation immediately visible; text rises 24px in 2–3 lines over 650ms; cargo resolves from a shallow mask. First scroll separates the central evidence panes and follows a source link into the dossier. No forced intro.','Inspect sample claim → /demo/cases/FC-208; Request a pilot → /pilot'),
('H02','The loss is visible. The evidence is scattered.','BOL in one inbox. Photos at the warehouse. Delivery evidence unresolved. A draft amount that does not match the invoice.','Cool silver-gray schematic route with four source islands; fictional origin/handoff/delivery, no real tracking.','Vertical entry: each island enters from its actual handoff direction, then connector draws; missing source remains a gap.','Why change → /why-change'),
('H03','Follow one shipment into review.','Open the BOL, inspect the delivery record, reconcile the draft value and assign the evidence chase.','One desktop horizontal evidence strip with fixed case label; four labeled stops.','Pinned only on wide/tall screens. Vertical scroll advances four stops; visible progress and Skip chapter. Each stop holds readable source+finding.','Open each document → dossier source pane'),
('H04','Keep the source. Show the uncertainty.','Original attachments, origin metadata and reviewer corrections stay distinct. Uncertain OCR becomes a task, not an invented delivery notation.','Deep graphite evidence vault; left document crop, center extracted field, right correction history.','Vertical layered reveal: source rises, field connects from right, uncertainty underline appears; scroll reverses visual layers without altering data.','Explore provenance → /platform'),
('H05','Five offers. One clear first test.','Start with Freight Desk. Evaluate rule tracking, reconciliation, reviewed packets and prevention reporting as separate offers.','Crisp white editorial product index; five bespoke mini-scenes and direct page links.','All names visible without horizontal interaction. One-time alternating 16–24px reveals; hover/focus highlights the owning workflow.','Five product routes + /products'),
('H06','Different roles. Explicit authority.','Cargo owner, 3PL agent and insurer have different responsibilities. Contracting or insurance counsel validates standing and permitted handling.','White and silver role topology; central analyst dossier, three distinct party geometries and separate counsel layer.','Nodes enter by role; solid/dashed connectors distinguish recorded/awaiting authority. Keyboard role selector gives same explanation.','Permissions → /trust'),
('H07','A review queue with a next action.','A. Chen owns FC-208’s evidence chase. The signed POD remains unresolved. The filing deadline remains Verify.','Full-width readable workbench on paper; no floating illegible dashboard collage.','Vertical stepper focuses source → discrepancy → assigned task → history. Actual clicks drive corrections; scroll only explains them.','Enter workbench → /demo/queue'),
('H08','A deadline needs a source.','Carrier, mode, contract, jurisdiction and rule owner belong beside every verified date. When applicability is unknown, the date stays unknown.','Archive-style rule card, version spine and timeline with an intentional blank slot.','A source slot slides open; no date “fills itself.” Reveal verification owner and missing contract label.','Rule FAQ → /resources/carrier-rules'),
('H09','Measure the audit against the workflow you already use.','FreightClaims, carrier portals, spreadsheets, TMS workflows and recovery firms already serve this market. Test whether the audit adds useful evidence or saves preparation work.','Neutral comparison matrix beside a sample audit comparison sheet; no winner trophy.','Rows reveal once; selected baseline emphasizes evaluation fields.','Compare workflows → /resources/compare-workflows'),
('H10','Test a 20-case bundle.','Proposed test price: $400 for a retrospective 20-case audit; a subsequent $8 per audited intake case is a separate hypothesis. Scope and authority come first.','Cool white and silver tray containing 20 case markers; calm commercial panel.','Case tray settles once, numbers appear at final value; never count up from zero.','Request a pilot → /pilot; Details → /pricing'),
('H11','Evidence before expansion.','Target 10 claims-manager interviews, two permissioned retrospective sets and one paid 20-case audit within 45 days. Track preparation time, corrections, deficiency returns and outcomes only where knowable.','Research scorecard with blank measured columns; synthetic report in a separate inset.','Vertical milestones reveal with labels “target,” not achieved. Chart includes unknown outcome cohort.','Evaluation → /results; methodology → resource page'),
('H12','Clear answers before a pilot.','Is this operating software? Who files? Which deadlines apply? Can I upload real documents? Is pricing final? What if my TMS already solves this?','Paper FAQ with a small context-specific evidence glyph per topic.','Accessible accordion; 180–240ms height/opacity transition or instant reduced motion.','Read detailed FAQ / Contact'),
('H13','Bring a workflow. Start with a scoped audit.','Tell us who owns claims, your case-volume range, carrier/mode and current software. Do not send claimant documents through this public concept.','Quiet closed dossier with one open review tab; contrast returns to graphite.','Text enters from below; CTA is immediately available. Footer remains ordinary readable layout.','Pilot / Request demo / Contact')]
section('home','07 / Homepage copy and scroll storyboard',p('This is the landing-copy baseline. The hero, sample case, five offers and commercial boundary must remain understandable with all motion disabled. Each chapter gets a different explanatory visual, with shared materials, typography and line conventions.')+''.join('<article class="chapter"><div class="eyebrow">'+code+'</div><h3>'+title+'</h3><p class="copy">'+copy+'</p>'+table(['Layer','Direction'],[['Visual / background',visual],['Motion',motion],['CTA / destination',cta]])+'</article>' for code,title,copy,visual,motion,cta in home)+box('Homepage target: about 8–10 minutes for a deliberate full read, with a 30–60 second scan path through hero, five offers, sample case and pilot. Do not force visitors through every animation to reach pricing or request a demo. Keep chapter anchors accessible from a compact contents control.'))

section('motion','08 / Motion system and interaction specification',p('Use Lenis and GSAP ScrollTrigger as progressive enhancement over native document flow. Motion tells the evidence story. It never changes claim data, grants authority or simulates a successful external action.')+table(['Sequence','Trigger / duration','Visible change','Reverse / exit','Mobile / reduced motion'],[
['Hero reveal','Page ready; 650–900ms total; no blocking preloader','Text from below, cargo from right via shallow mask, evidence lines last. CTA is available immediately.','Entrance does not replay on tiny scroll changes.','Static hero scene; text already visible; no smooth scrolling for reduced motion.'],
['Cargo → dossier','Hero top to roughly +0.8 viewport on desktop','Container panel pivots ≤12°; transparent sheets spread ≤80px; crossfade to editable UI scene.','Scrubbed scene reverses; exit hands off to normal document flow.','One still image plus adjacent readable summary; no geometry morph required.'],
['Horizontal evidence chapter','Wide ≥1100px and height ≥760px; initial design budget 220–280vh, tune after reading test','Four stops: BOL → POD gap → invoice discrepancy → reviewer task. x translation derives from actual scrollWidth minus container width.','Visible skip anchor; exit at end; reverse retraces without clearing completed reader actions.','Stack four panels vertically. No sticky horizontal content, forced drag or hidden offscreen reading.'],
['Provenance layers','Section entry / 0–1 local progress','Source crop appears first; field highlight and lineage connect; correction history comes last.','Scrubbed visual reassembles predictably. Data history remains unchanged.','Complete still with numbered reading order and an accessible table.'],
['Product family','Entry once, ~450ms per panel; stagger ≤80ms','Alternate shallow x±24px/y24px, never every paragraph flying from a different edge.','Remain visible after entry.','No transform; all five names and links shown.'],
['Party diagram','Entry plus role selection','Paths draw to node ports; selected role lights its permitted actions. Counsel bracket remains separate.','Selection persists; scrolling does not change permissions.','Stack roles with labeled responsibilities and status.'],
['Amount reconciliation','Scroll chapter entry; explicit click to inspect','Draft and invoice align; discrepancy appears; original remains visible after a reviewer correction.','Scroll reverses explanatory movement only. Undo demo correction is a separate control.','Side-by-side where readable, otherwise stacked labeled values.'],
['Rule timeline','Entry and source-card expansion','Owner/version/applicability fields reveal. Unknown date stays Verify.','No automatic completion state.','Simple expandable source card; same evidence.'],
['Report chart','Once on entry, 400ms bar growth from zero height','Final known synthetic amounts with source labels; unknown records remain a distinct count.','Final values remain visible.','Immediate final bars/table; no animated numbers.'],
['Page transitions','Route navigation, max 200ms opacity','Keep navigation stable; new page heading receives focus when appropriate.','No full-screen curtain on every route.','Instant on reduced motion.'],
['Forms / sign-in / legal','Ordinary interactions only','Focus, validation, loading and truthful result states.','Back/forward and reload preserve expected navigation.','No pinning or cinematic distractions.']
])+p('<strong>Hover/focus family:</strong> buttons use a 180–220ms surface wipe and 4px arrow travel; product cards reveal an edge rail and highlight their actual mechanism; evidence cards outline the exact source field; diagram role controls highlight connected actions; resource links draw a short underline. Essential text is always visible. Avoid universal tilt, magnetic targets, cursor replacements and hover-only explanations.')+p('<strong>Implementation contract:</strong> use one Lenis instance and one RAF driver. The official '+a('https://github.com/darkroomengineering/lenis','Lenis integration')+' connects its scroll event to ScrollTrigger.update and calls lenis.raf(time × 1000) from GSAP’s ticker. Do not also start a second autoRAF loop. Use '+a('https://gsap.com/docs/v3/GSAP/gsap.matchMedia()/','gsap.matchMedia')+' for breakpoints and motion preferences, revert scoped animations, remove ticker callbacks and destroy Lenis on teardown. Recompute measurements after fonts/images settle and after responsive changes. '+a('https://gsap.com/docs/v3/Plugins/ScrollTrigger/','ScrollTrigger documentation')+' is the pin/scrub reference.')+p('<strong>Reading and accessibility:</strong> maintain semantic headings, DOM reading order, native anchors and scroll-margin below the sticky header. Text must be visible before enhancement and on script failure. Avoid animating long text with screen-reader-duplicated split spans. If split text is used, provide one accessible phrase and aria-hide decorative fragments. Pause ongoing effects offscreen/when hidden; include pause/skip for any long scene. Follow '+a('https://gsap.com/resources/a11y/','GSAP accessibility guidance')+'.')+p('<strong>Performance targets for the later build:</strong> LCP ≤2.5s, INP ≤200ms and CLS ≤0.1 at the 75th percentile are targets, not measured results here. Load a lightweight hero poster before optional 3D; lazy-load below-fold media; compress images; reserve dimensions; cap active timelines; prefer transforms/opacity and editable SVG over expensive canvas scenes. Test mid-range mobile hardware and low-power mode.'))

