section('pilot','12 / Pilot, demand experiment and measurement',p('<strong>Proposed price copy:</strong> “Test a retrospective 20-case evidence audit for $400. A subsequent $8 per audited intake case is a pricing hypothesis. These are proposed test prices, not current rates, accepted offers or recovery promises. Scope, data authority and the approved review workflow must be agreed first.” No checkout, payment collection or artificial plan tiers.')+p('<strong>45-day validation target:</strong> at least 10 claims-manager interviews, two permissioned retrospective case sets and one paid 20-case audit. The clock starts when the validation program is actually launched. No progress is marked achieved in this plan.')+table(['Phase','Work','Evidence required'],[
['Days 1–10','Interview claims managers, analysts, contracting/insurance counsel and current workflow owners.','Who owns write-offs and claims budget; case frequency; current software/configuration; recurring failure points; authority to share data.'],
['Days 11–20','Secure two authorized retrospective sets of closed and open cases; scope one carrier/mode.','Document/data rights, source access, standing review, named rule owner, confidentiality/retention terms and approved handling.'],
['Days 21–35','Run matched baseline versus audit comparison; adjudicate incremental useful gaps and reviewer burden.','Time logs, corrections, source-linked findings, false flags, deficiency returns and known outcomes; comparable case mix.'],
['Days 36–45','Seek one paid bundle from an accountable buyer and decide.','Actual agreed/paid commitment outside the demo, named manager, approved submission pathway and evidence of incremental value.']
])+p('Retrospective recovery comparisons are descriptive, not proof that the audit caused recovery. Open cases need a follow-up period; unknown outcomes remain unknown. Compare the same cases or carefully matched cases; record reviewer learning effects and current-platform configuration. Proposed improvement thresholds should be agreed with the buyer before reviewing results, rather than invented after the pilot.')+table(['Tracking field','Worksheet column','How to use'],[[label,k,g] for k,label,g in pilot_fields])+p('These fields also satisfy the later Notion tracking schema. The downloadable worksheet JSON contains 20 blank case slots plus aggregation guidance; it is not a results dataset.')+table(['Decision','Gate'],[
['Proceed','Paid audits surface adjudicated incremental gaps versus FreightClaims/manual/current TMS, the buyer can lawfully share documents, and a named manager owns the approved workflow.'],
['Pivot','Evidence intake is commoditized but packaging/root-cause reporting has a separately accountable prevention buyer and budget; test Freight Report independently.'],
['Stop','Claimant authority or required contract access fails; data cannot lawfully be shared; no incremental useful value; or no accountable willingness to pay.'],
['Expansion hypothesis','After evidence of value in one carrier/mode, test other modes, subsidiaries and prevention reporting. Legal/insurance services remain adjacent only where properly licensed and permitted.'],
['Revenue logic','Paid case volume and retained contracts drive revenue. Total damaged-freight value is not revenue. A million-dollar business is a hypothesis to validate, not a headline or forecast.']
]))

section('conversion','13 / Acquisition, forms and analytics',table(['Channel / experiment','Content / action','Commitment measured'],[
['Shipper transportation teams / claims managers','Document-gap anatomy of FC-208; ask who owns write-offs and repeated deficiency work.','Named claims manager with budget and an authorized sample pathway.'],
['3PL account managers','Delegation and evidence-chase story; separate agent from claimant.','Introductions to the actual budget/authority owner.'],
['Cargo insurance brokers / freight audit consultants','A checklist for evaluating evidence preparation and existing tools; no implied partnership.','Qualified buyer introduction and explicit handling scope.'],
['Warehouse OS&D teams','Show missing/illegible POD and photo provenance before downstream review.','Workflow evidence and handoff owner, not an assumption they control the budget.'],
['LinkedIn plan','Original fictional document-gap post plus manual-vs-existing-FreightClaims comparison checklist. Ask who can authorize pilot data.','Qualified research conversation and paid-bundle request. No posts sent in this deliverable.'],
['Ad creative A','“The POD was there. The signature was not readable.” Show original synthetic source crop and review task.','Paid-audit intent and qualified form completion.'],
['Ad creative B','“A $240 discrepancy before the packet leaves review.” Show synthetic draft/invoice comparison, not recovered money.','Same qualification path; compare cohorts using campaign tags.'],
['Spend rule','Any traffic test needs a separately approved cap, audience, creative and campaign tags before launch.','No ad spend, account creation or outreach is authorized by this planning artifact.']
])+p('<strong>Pilot form fields:</strong> work email, name, organization, role, claims volume range, carrier/mode, current software, selected module, buyer/budget authority, ability to authorize data use, and consent to follow up. No file input. Avoid inviting sensitive case details in free text. Guided-demo form offers all five products plus “full platform”; contact form collects minimal message context.')+table(['State','Exact or baseline UI copy'],[
['Persistent disclosure','“Concept preview. No real claimant documents or payments are accepted here.”'],
['Consent','“I agree to be contacted about this pilot request and have read the privacy notice.” Separate optional marketing consent, unchecked by default.'],
['Authority question','“Are you authorized to discuss a pilot and arrange a separate review of data-sharing permissions?” Options: Yes / Need another owner / Exploring. This is not a legal standing determination.'],
['Before integration','“This form is a preview and is not connected. Nothing will be sent.” Use a preview action, not a fake Send button.'],
['Validation error','“Enter a work email so we can respond.” / “Choose the product or workflow you want to discuss.”'],
['Connected success (future only)','“Your request was received. We will review scope and contact the named owner. Do not send documents until an approved channel and agreement are in place.” Do not invent a response SLA.'],
['Delivery failure','“Your request was not sent. Please try again.” Preserve nonsensitive form entries for correction.'],
['Sign-in concept','“Workspace access is not available in this concept preview. Explore the synthetic demo or request access.” Never collect a real password in an unconnected prototype.'],
['Privacy draft','Explain controller/contact, purposes, data categories, lawful processing basis where relevant, retention/deletion, vendors, location, user choices and contact route before launch. Mark unknown business details as unresolved; do not publish a finished legal promise from assumptions.']
])+p('<strong>Analytics plan:</strong> consent-aware events <code>sample_open</code>, <code>missing_evidence_drilldown</code>, <code>source_view</code>, <code>demo_correction_recorded</code>, <code>product_view</code>, <code>pilot_request_started</code>, <code>paid_audit_form_completion</code> and <code>guided_demo_request</code>. Properties: page, proposed module, campaign/source, synthetic case ID and event version. Do not log document text, emails or claimant data in analytics. In a local preview, events are diagnostic only. Form completion means a request, not payment, demand proof or a successful pilot.')+p('<strong>Acceptance event:</strong> record a real qualified buyer commitment and later paid-bundle evidence in a separate authorized business process. CTR, scroll depth, sample clicks and simulated completions are engagement signals only.'))

