section('handoff','15 / Acceptance, unresolved decisions and build handoff',table(['Gate','Acceptance evidence for later implementation'],[
['Content and IA','All five products on home, mega menu, product index, individual pages and demo intake. Every planned route has purposeful content and working navigation.'],
['Visual selection','Claim Atlas selected with cream removed; use the crisp-white v2 target before creating final logo/vector/icon kit, typography tokens, responsive wireframes and complete page designs. Do not silently mix generated logos or UI data.'],
['Product truth','Persistent DEMO / CONCEPT PREVIEW badges; no real documents/payments; no real carrier approval; source uncertainty and role boundaries remain visible in every viewport.'],
['Functional demo','Filter queue, open FC-208, inspect original evidence, assign/review a task, record a synthetic correction with history, view rule source gap, generate labeled sample export, inspect report and reset demo.'],
['Data consistency','Queue counts match ten records; 12×240=$2,880, 12×220=$2,640, delta=$240; source shipment total=$22,000. Known-outcome cohort count and totals match fixtures. Null is never silently zero.'],
['Responsive captures','Real browser capture of queue, dossier/source/reviewer and report at 1440px desktop and 390px mobile. Product dossier target 1440×900. Verify labels and figures at 100% zoom.'],
['Motion','Down/up scroll, short-screen pin exit, skip, route cleanup, anchor jumps, reload, resize, native keyboard/touch and reduced motion. No permanently hidden text or uncapped looping visuals.'],
['Accessibility','Semantic landmarks/headings, focus order/return, labeled icon buttons, sufficient contrast, status beyond color, accessible chart summary/table, usable forms and error feedback.'],
['Forms/auth','Clearly distinguish preview from connected delivery. Test genuine form integration only in an authorized test environment; do not send test outreach or real credentials from the demo.'],
['Assets/performance','Optimized media and local dependencies; font licenses retained; no template artifacts, personal file paths, secrets, fictitious logos or unauthorized stock/customer photos in production.'],
['Launch','Production build and meaningful checks, repository handoff, Vercel deployment if authorized, custom domain after ownership verification, then review actual deployed pages. No check marked passed from code inspection alone.']
])+p('<strong>Open decisions that do not block this planning deliverable:</strong> final module-name approval/trademark review; legal business entity and contact details; real domain ownership; LinkedIn/Crunchbase URLs; named pilot carrier/mode and contract owner; actual data/standing permissions; form/privacy implementation; repository/deployment target; whether any integrations will be built. None is silently assumed.')+box('<strong>Historical domain note:</strong> the supplied draft says freighttrestle.com returned RDAP 404 at a prior research time, was unpurchased and lacked trademark clearance. That is a historical assertion in the source brief, not current domain evidence. It does not establish availability or rights for FreightClaimKit. Recheck any chosen name/domain through the appropriate registrar and legal process before use.')+p('<strong>Deliverable status:</strong> the research, page architecture, copy baseline, motion plan, three visual studies, coverage register, ten-record fixture and blank pilot worksheet are delivered. Final brand asset production, production website, functional prototype, actual 1440/390 product captures, live forms, repository, deployment and domain remain future execution. The generated visual studies are explicitly excluded from implementation screenshot acceptance.')+p('<strong>Recommended next production sequence:</strong> carry the selected crisp-white Claim Atlas target into identity → finalize identity → wireframe all page families → create functional synthetic dossier screens → compose high-fidelity homepage and five product heroes → implement responsive routes and motion → QA → authorized launch. The first product proof should be an inspectable source-to-review action, not an ornamental dashboard animation.'))

# Homepage and resource FAQ answer baseline.
faq = table(['Question','Answer baseline'],[
('Is FreightClaimKit operating software?','This is a research-stage website and synthetic product concept. Availability, demand, integrations and commercial acceptance are not established.'),
('What is the first pilot?','A permissioned retrospective evidence audit for a scoped 20-case bundle, initially one carrier/mode. A claims manager must own the budget and approved workflow.'),
('Which claim deadline applies?','The applicable carrier, mode, contract, jurisdiction and triggering event must be verified by the named rule owner. If the source or applicability is unknown, the deadline remains Verify.'),
('Does the demo file a claim?','No. It demonstrates evidence review and human-reviewed synthetic export. Any future external submission must be approved by the authorized claimant through a permitted workflow.'),
('Can a 3PL or insurer act for the cargo owner?','Only where the relevant authority and permitted handling have been established. The demo separates the parties and does not infer standing from a role label.'),
('Can I upload real claimant documents?','No. The public demo uses bundled synthetic records only. Any future retrospective pilot requires a separate approved data channel and permission process.'),
('What happens when OCR is uncertain?','The original source remains visible and the field becomes a reviewer task. The system must not invent signatures, dates or delivery notations.'),
('Does an audit guarantee recovery?','No. Completeness and source integrity do not determine liability, coverage, recoverability or settlement. Known outcomes are tracked only with supporting evidence.'),
('How is this different from FreightClaims or our TMS?','That is the pilot question. Compare the proposed audit against the existing configured workflow on authorized cases, including useful additional gaps, corrections and preparation work.'),
('Are the prices final?','No. $400 for a retrospective 20-case bundle and a subsequent $8 per audited intake case are test hypotheses. The concept has no checkout or accepted current pricing.'),
('Are carrier or TMS integrations live?','None has been demonstrated for this concept. Workflow-fit diagrams describe proposed boundaries and approved external paths, not operating connections.'),
('What happens after I request a pilot?','In a connected future form, the team reviews scope, buyer ownership and data authority before any agreement or document exchange. The present planning deliverable does not send requests.')])
idx = next(i for i,x in enumerate(sections) if x[0]=='conversion')
sections[idx]=(sections[idx][0],sections[idx][1],sections[idx][2]+'<h3>FAQ copy baseline</h3>'+faq)

